{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/s16SendableMetatypeP"],"type":"conformsTo","title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships"}],"sections":[],"kind":"symbol","identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"metadata":{"title":"RadixHeap","role":"symbol","modules":[{"name":"PriorityQueueModule"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"RadixHeap.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap.swift#L17"},"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixHeap","kind":"identifier"}],"symbolKind":"struct","roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:19PriorityQueueModule9RadixHeapV","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixHeap"}]},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"RadixHeap"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Value"},{"kind":"text","text":">"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The radix heap of Ahuja, Mehlhorn, Orlin and Tarjan, in the form with one bucket per bit:"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"bucket "},{"code":"b","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" holds the keys whose highest bit differing from the last key removed is bit"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"b - 1","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", and bucket 0 the keys equal to it. "},{"code":"insert","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1). "},{"code":"popMin()","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is O(1) when bucket 0"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"holds a pair; otherwise it empties the lowest nonempty bucket into lower ones. A pair moves"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"only to lower buckets, so it moves at most "},{"code":"UInt.bitWidth","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" times, and for keys spread over a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range of "},{"code":"C","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" at most log₂ C + 1 times: amortized O(log C) a pop."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use it where keys never go below the last one removed, as in Dijkstra’s algorithm with","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer weights. It has no decrease-key: insert the value again with the lower key and skip","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"the stale pair when it comes out. Values with equal keys leave in an unspecified order.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The queue is not a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence"},{"type":"text","text":". Storage is an array of bucket arrays, copied on write."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"text":"A monotone min-priority queue of values with nonnegative integer keys, where no key inserted","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"is below the last key removed.","type":"text"}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/priorityqueuemodule\/radixheap"]}],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/init()"],"title":"Initializers","generated":true,"anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/count","doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/isEmpty","doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/lastRemovedKey"],"title":"Instance Properties","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Properties"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/insert(_:key:)","doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/popMin()","doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/removeMin()"],"title":"Instance Methods","generated":true,"anchor":"Instance-Methods"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/Element"],"title":"Type Aliases","generated":true,"anchor":"Type-Aliases"}],"references":{"doc://PriorityQueueModule/documentation/PriorityQueueModule/RadixHeap/removeMin()":{"type":"topic","title":"removeMin()","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule\/RadixHeap\/removeMin()","abstract":[{"text":"Removes and returns a pair with the lowest key. O(log C) amortized.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/priorityqueuemodule\/radixheap\/removemin()","role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"removeMin","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"RadixHeap","preciseIdentifier":"s:19PriorityQueueModule9RadixHeapV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Value","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">.","kind":"text"},{"text":"Element","preciseIdentifier":"s:19PriorityQueueModule9RadixHeapV7Elementa","kind":"typeIdentifier"}]},"doc://PriorityQueueModule/documentation/PriorityQueueModule":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/PriorityQueueModule\/documentation\/PriorityQueueModule","url":"\/documentation\/priorityqueuemodule","kind":"symbol","title":"PriorityQueueModule","type":"topic","abstract":[],"role":"collection"},"doc://PriorityQueueModule/documentation/PriorityQueueModule/RadixHeap":{"kind":"symbol","title":